__pycache__
*.pyc
metastore_db
# Anchored deliberately. A bare `tags` pattern matches ANY path segment named
# `tags`, including `.git/refs/tags/` -- and rattler-build's path-source copy
# honours .gitignore, so it silently dropped every loose tag ref from the
# build sandbox. versioneer then fell through to `git describe` against the
# handful of tags that happened to be in .git/packed-refs and baked a wrong
# __version__ into the wheel: toksearch 2.11.0 shipped
# `0+untagged.208.g827f651` (CI, where all refs are loose) and built as
# `2.2.3+156.g827f651` locally. The conda metadata was right either way,
# because that comes from PKG_VERSION derived in the real repo.
# `/tags` matches only a ctags file at the repo root, which is all this was
# ever meant to ignore.
/tags
*.so
build
dist
envs
*.egg-info
toksearch.orig
.eggs


